1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,280
In this last discussion, in order to close off the chapter,

2
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:04,900
we're gonna cover both cardiomyopathy and cardiac tumors.

3
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:07,900
Cardiomyopathy refers to myocardial diseases

4
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:09,820
that result in cardiac dysfunction.

5
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:12,560
The first is called dilated cardiomyopathy.

6
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:14,740
In this particular case, you get dilatation

7
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:16,520
of all four chambers of the heart.

8
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:18,960
This is the most common form of cardiomyopathy.

9
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:20,240
Here's what it looks like.

10
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:23,260
You get massively dilated chambers of the heart.

11
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:24,860
You can look at the two atria here,

12
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:26,740
and you can look at the two ventricles here.

13
00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:29,260
Now, the problem with this is that it's gonna result

14
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:30,660
in a systolic dysfunction.

15
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:34,640
If you stretch the heart so that it's no longer able

16
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:38,120
to contract properly, that massive stretching of the heart

17
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:40,300
is then going to result in a problem with systole,

18
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,440
so that you won't be able to empty the heart.

19
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:43,980
And, of course, that's gonna result

20
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:46,040
in biventricular congestive heart failure.

21
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:48,000
Both the left and the right sides

22
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,920
are both going to fail together.

23
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:52,420
The complications include mitral

24
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:54,580
and tricuspid valve regurgitation.

25
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,020
Imagine that if this is the heart here,

26
00:00:57,020 --> 00:01:00,280
and you've got the right atrium, right ventricle,

27
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:03,380
left atrium, left ventricle.

28
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:06,300
As you stretch this heart, you're going to be stretching

29
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:08,800
the mitral valve and the tricuspid valve.

30
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:10,160
Again, this is the tricuspid.

31
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:12,240
And then you'll stretch the mitral valve.

32
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:14,320
And again, that stretching is gonna result

33
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:15,980
in regurgitation of those valves.

34
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:18,780
So, number one, you get systolic dysfunction.

35
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:20,480
And number two, you're gonna get stretching

36
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,320
and regurgitation of these valves.

37
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:24,600
Another complication would be arrhythmia.

38
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:26,780
The way I think about this is that as you stretch the heart,

39
00:01:26,860 --> 00:01:29,080
you're also stretching the conduction systems of the heart.

40
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:31,620
And so you're gonna start getting funny conductions

41
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:33,580
across that system, giving you arrhythmias.

42
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:36,500
Now, most commonly, dilated cardiomyopathy

43
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:37,540
is idiopathic.

44
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:38,500
We don't know the cause.

45
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:40,940
But some very high-yield causes to be aware of

46
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:42,220
include genetic mutations.

47
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:45,220
Usually, the most common genetic mutation

48
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:46,480
would be autosomal dominant.

49
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,020
Myocarditis can do it.

50
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:49,960
The most common bug to cause myocarditis

51
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:51,120
would be Coxsackievirus.

52
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:54,160
That results in a lymphocytic infiltrate in the myocardium.

53
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:55,720
The patients get chest pain.

54
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:57,540
They can get arrhythmia with sudden death.

55
00:01:57,640 --> 00:01:58,580
They can get heart failure.

56
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:01,020
If they manage to survive the myocarditis,

57
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:02,440
then one of the late complications

58
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:04,340
is dilated cardiomyopathy.

59
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:06,480
Alcohol abuse, very high-yield,

60
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:08,180
can cause a dilated cardiomyopathy.

61
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:10,440
There are some drugs that can cause it.

62
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:12,880
For example, doxorubicin can result

63
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:15,360
in a dilated cardiomyopathy, and so can cocaine.

64
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:18,460
And then finally, particularly high-yield, is pregnancy.

65
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:21,620
Women who are pregnant either late in the third trimester

66
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:23,320
or, for example, soon after birth

67
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:27,560
can develop heart failure due to a dilated cardiomyopathy.

68
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:30,260
Now, here's a picture of myocarditis

69
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:32,060
just to remind you of myocarditis

70
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:33,820
as a cause of dilated cardiomyopathy.

71
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:35,980
You can see all the lymphocytes present

72
00:02:35,980 --> 00:02:37,960
within the myocardium.

73
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:41,380
Again, myocarditis, most common cause, Coxsackievirus.

74
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:44,220
And this can result in death during the acute phase,

75
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:46,780
or if the patient survived, can eventually result

76
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:48,700
in a dilated cardiomyopathy.

77
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:51,120
Now, the treatment for dilated cardiomyopathy

78
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:51,840
is transplant.

79
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:54,200
There's no way to fix that dilated heart.

80
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:56,660
Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy is when you get

81
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:58,900
massive hypertrophy of the left ventricle.

82
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:01,840
The most common cause, and of course, very high-yield,

83
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:03,580
is that you get genetic mutations

84
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:06,300
in the sarcomere proteins, high-yield,

85
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,520
most commonly autosomal dominant.

86
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:10,120
Now, these patients are gonna get

87
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:11,400
decreased cardiac output.

88
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:13,900
And the reason is because the hypertrophy

89
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:15,820
makes the heart wall so tight

90
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:17,440
that you can't fill the heart anymore.

91
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,860
Basically, the wall becomes so full of muscle

92
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:21,100
that you lose compliance.

93
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:23,420
And so you get a diastolic dysfunction

94
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:24,600
where you can't fill the heart.

95
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:27,360
At the same time, the patients can get sudden death

96
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:29,260
due to ventricular arrhythmias.

97
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,340
This is the most common cause of sudden death

98
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:32,960
in young athletes, and we're all aware

99
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:34,800
of those athletes that are playing on the field

100
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,080
and all of a sudden pass out.

101
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,600
And that's classically due

102
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:39,400
to a hypertrophic cardiomyopathy.

103
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:42,340
Another complication is syncope with exercise.

104
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:44,220
We can illustrate that very quickly.

105
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:46,520
Right atrium, right ventricle,

106
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:48,740
left atrium, left ventricle.

107
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,420
And the idea here is that you get

108
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:51,780
this preferential involvement

109
00:03:51,780 --> 00:03:53,780
of the intraventricular septum

110
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:56,120
right beneath the aortic valve.

111
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:58,200
Now, this is basically going to create

112
00:03:58,200 --> 00:03:59,880
almost like a relative block,

113
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:01,480
the same way that aortic stenosis

114
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,300
would create a block.

115
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:04,000
This would create a relative block

116
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,220
so that you wouldn't be able to get

117
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:07,780
blood across this very well.

118
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:09,720
And that would then present with syncope

119
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:10,640
during exercise.

120
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,340
So that's basically,

121
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:14,040
you get a functional aortic stenosis.

122
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:15,920
Now, if biopsy were performed,

123
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:17,740
you would see myofiber hypertrophy

124
00:04:17,740 --> 00:04:18,780
with disarray.

125
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:20,900
And this is a particularly high-yield image,

126
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:22,260
so let me just take you through it.

127
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:24,260
Normally, when you look at the myocytes,

128
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:26,480
they should all sort of be lined up very nicely

129
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,660
and in parallel.

130
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:29,640
However, notice here that there's all this

131
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:31,480
disorganization with the myocytes

132
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:33,300
sort of going in every different direction.

133
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:35,740
And that's called myocyte disarray.

134
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:37,600
And it's the classic finding

135
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:39,560
in hypertrophic cardiomyopathy.

136
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:42,700
Restrictive cardiomyopathy is when you are restricted

137
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:44,160
from filling the heart.

138
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:46,500
And that's because there's a decreased compliance

139
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:48,420
of the ventricular endomyocardium.

140
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:49,760
Again, you can't fill,

141
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:51,600
so there'll be a diastolic problem.

142
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:53,060
Now, what are the causes?

143
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:54,520
Amyloid can fill the heart,

144
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:56,500
making the heart very difficult to expand.

145
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:57,940
And so, therefore, that would result

146
00:04:57,940 --> 00:04:59,560
in a restrictive cardiomyopathy.

147
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:02,680
Sarcoidosis, the granulomas of sarcoidosis

148
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:03,900
can get into the wall of the heart,

149
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,780
making it difficult to expand,

150
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:08,240
resulting in a restrictive cardiomyopathy.

151
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:11,140
Hemochromatosis, if iron gets into the wall of the heart,

152
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:12,240
it can do the same thing.

153
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:13,740
There's an interesting disorder

154
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:16,320
called endocardiofibroelastosis.

155
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:19,100
And this is when patients have a dense layer

156
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:22,280
of fibrosis and elastic tissue in the endocardium.

157
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:24,000
Now, remember that the layers of the heart

158
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,600
are the endocardium, and then the myocardium,

159
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:27,940
and then the epicardium.

160
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:30,000
Now, imagine if this endocardium

161
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,800
becomes massively fibrosed

162
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:34,300
and thickened with elastic tissue.

163
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:36,200
You won't be able to stretch this

164
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:37,660
when you expand the heart open,

165
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:39,220
and so that would then result

166
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:41,300
in a restrictive cardiomyopathy.

167
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:43,980
Now, I should note that endocardiofibroelastosis

168
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:45,680
would classically be seen in children,

169
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:47,620
and so it's one of the rare causes

170
00:05:47,620 --> 00:05:50,020
of a restrictive cardiomyopathy in children.

171
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:52,580
Another cause of restrictive cardiomyopathy

172
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:53,580
is Loeffler syndrome.

173
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,280
The idea here is that you get

174
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:57,460
an eosinophilic infiltrate with inflammation

175
00:05:57,460 --> 00:06:00,060
within the wall of the heart, again with eosinophils,

176
00:06:00,380 --> 00:06:03,760
and that results in fibrosis of the endomyocardium,

177
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:05,740
both the endocardium and the myocardium.

178
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:08,360
Of course, this fibrosis would then make it difficult

179
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:09,900
for the heart to expand and fill,

180
00:06:10,260 --> 00:06:12,480
and so you'd get a restrictive cardiomyopathy.

181
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:14,460
Patients with a restrictive cardiomyopathy

182
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:16,120
will present with congestive heart failure,

183
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:17,640
and again, that's because they're not able

184
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,500
to fill the heart, so the blood will back up

185
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:20,480
behind the heart.

186
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:22,480
And the classic finding on EKG,

187
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:23,780
because you've got all this material

188
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:26,640
on the wall of the heart will be low-voltage EKG

189
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:29,140
with diminished QRS amplitudes,

190
00:06:29,300 --> 00:06:30,640
and that's important to note as well.

191
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:32,520
The final section of this chapter

192
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:33,680
deals with cardiac tumors.

193
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:34,760
It's very straightforward.

194
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:37,240
The first cardiac tumor is called a myxoma.

195
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:39,640
This is a mesenchymal proliferation

196
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,180
where you get a gelatinous appearance to the tumor.

197
00:06:42,580 --> 00:06:44,900
On histology, it shows abundant ground substance,

198
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:46,620
and that's what makes it look so gelatinous,

199
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:50,380
and this is the most common primary cardiac tumor in adults.

200
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:51,740
Remember that in adults,

201
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:56,780
they're not going to be able to produce a tumor,

202
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:58,340
so the only real tumor of the heart

203
00:06:58,340 --> 00:06:59,180
that you're going to get

204
00:06:59,180 --> 00:07:02,260
is going to be a tumor of the mesenchymal connective tissue.

205
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:03,960
Again, that's called a myxoma.

206
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,740
Now, this tumor normally grows in the left atrium

207
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:08,040
as a pedunculated mass,

208
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:10,400
and it can cause syncope due to obstruction

209
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:11,260
of the mitral valve.

210
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:13,220
Let's briefly illustrate this.

211
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:14,400
Here's a picture of the heart.

212
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:16,540
Again, these are our four chambers,

213
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:18,160
and in this particular case,

214
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:19,500
we're in the left atrium,

215
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:21,500
and you've got this pedunculated mass.

216
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:23,740
Pedunculated means it grows off a little stalk.

217
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:25,780
And so you've got this pedunculated mass.

218
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:29,400
Now, this mass could easily block the mitral valve here,

219
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,080
and were it to block the mitral valve,

220
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,800
that would block the blood flow through the heart.

221
00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:34,980
Of course, blood would not go to the brain then,

222
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,160
and so you'd get syncope.

223
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:38,060
And so that's why we say here in the book

224
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:40,120
that it causes syncope due to obstruction

225
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:41,380
of the mitral valve.

226
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:43,500
The next tumor is rhabdomyoma.

227
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:45,220
Rhabdomyoma means striated muscle,

228
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:46,320
and oma means mass.

229
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:49,380
This is a benign hemartoma of cardiac muscle.

230
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:52,560
It's the most common primary cardiac tumor in children.

231
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:55,480
High yield, it's associated with tuberous sclerosis.

232
00:07:55,660 --> 00:07:56,620
That is very high yield,

233
00:07:57,020 --> 00:07:59,080
and it usually arises in the ventricle.

234
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:01,560
Now, the last discussion about cardiac tumors

235
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:02,700
involves metastases.

236
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:05,120
Metastases to the heart is more common

237
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,140
than primary tumors.

238
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:08,140
And common metastases to the heart,

239
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:10,300
they include breast and lung cancer,

240
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:11,660
melanoma, and lymphoma.

241
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:13,780
These are the tumors that love to go to the heart.

242
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,020
When they go to the heart,

243
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:16,660
they usually go to the pericardium,

244
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:19,540
and it results in a pericardial effusion.

245
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,920
And so that closes off both the section and this chapter.

